   "source": [
    "# <span style=\"color:red\"> Lecture 8: Pandas Operations and Data Manipulation </span>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e9e980d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<font size = \"4\">\n",
    "\n",
    "Topics we should be familiar up to this point:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Object Types**: int, float, str, lists, arrays,<br>\n",
    "booleans, pandas dataframes\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "- If/elif/else statements and loops\n",
    "\n",
    "- Functions (both built-in and user defined)\n",
    "\n",
    "If there are any of these topics you need help <br>\n",
    " understanding, don't be afraid to come to office hours!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "69b69e45",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<font size = \"4\">\n",
    "\n",
    "This lecture:\n",
    "\n",
    "- We will take a closer look at the `Pandas` library\n",
    "\n",
    "- A lot of new object types and functions/methods\n",
    "\n",
    "- We should keep the basic programming ideas listed above in mind"
   ]
  },
  {
